## Bazaar database migrations

Run Alembic commands from `backend/`. The migration environment reads
`DATABASE_URL` and the other backend settings using the same configuration as
the application; if unset, the database defaults to `backend/bazaar.db`.

Apply all pending migrations before starting the API:

```bash
uv run alembic upgrade head
```

Create a revision after changing SQLAlchemy models:

```bash
uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"
```

Review generated revisions before applying them. The initial commerce
migration also adds the `customer` role to existing user rows while preserving
their accounts. Do not edit an already-applied migration; create a new revision
instead.